# Engineering Standards & Architecture Guardrails

## 1. Semantic Git (Conventional Commits)
- Format: `<type>(<scope>): <short summary in imperative mood>`
- Permitted types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`.
- Strict rule: Commit messages must explain the *why* and *what*, avoiding vague descriptions like "update code".

## 2. Clean Code & Simplicity
- Follow Single Responsibility Principle (SRP) and DRY without premature abstraction.
- Functions must be concise (< 30 lines where practical), self-documenting, and avoid deep nesting (> 3 levels).
- Avoid magic numbers and strings: define named constants.
- Handle edge cases, errors, and invalid states explicitly (never swallow exceptions silently).

## 3. UI Component Standards (Shadcn UI & Skill UI Principles)
- Prefer accessible, composable, and unstyled/primitives-first component architecture.
- Every interactive element must have clear focus rings, accessible labels (`aria-*`), and distinct hover/active states.
- Avoid duplicate layout utility noise; extract reusable UI patterns into clean components.

## 4. Strict TypeScript Standards (Matt Pocock Style)
- Enable strict mode; never use `any` unless explicitly documenting an untypable boundary.
- Prefer explicit return types on public boundaries and exported functions.
- Use discriminated unions for modeling state machines and finite statuses.
- Use `satisfies` and `as const` for strict literal type inferences.

## 5. Browser Automation & Testing Guardrails (Browser-Use)
- Ensure all interactive dashboard elements have stable, predictable `id` and `data-testid` attributes.
- State changes must be observable via DOM attributes or explicit text content to facilitate automated verification.

## 6. Code Graph & Context Management (Context7 & Sourcegraph Principles)
- Keep dependencies explicit and modular.
- Organize code by domain/feature boundaries rather than arbitrary technical buckets.
- High-level orchestrators must not leak implementation details of low-level drivers.

## 7. Data Layer & Integrations (Supabase / Firebase Realtime / Strix)
- Enforce strict schemas and database validation rules.
- Gracefully handle offline states, network latency, timeouts, and reconnects without blocking the main event loop.
- Decouple telemetry ingestion from event logging and control pipelines.
